1024 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[1 .8 .25]/P 210 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[88.43832 397.64756 238.32244 397.64756 88.43832 386.89 238.32244 386.89]/Rect[85.90266 386.21769 240.8581 398.3199]/AP<</N 1025 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(This exhibit is mislabelled and the figures are wrong. The series is labelled core PCE, but none of the three points is a core-PCE year-on-year value. Core PCE peaked at ~5.6% \(Feb 2022\), not 6.1% \(6.1% is a headline-PCE-era figure; headline peaked ~7% mid-2022\). Q4 2023 core PCE was ~2.9%, not 2.1% \(2.1% looks like a quarterly-annualised rate\). And the latest core PCE was ~3.3% y/y \(April 2026\), not 4.4% \(4.4% is the annualised quarterly core rate, not the y/y level the chart claims to show\). So the chart mixes three different measures; restate all three as core-PCE y/y \(~5.6% / ~2.9% / ~3.3%\) or relabel the series. Minor, same paragraph: the 5.25-5.50% peak was set in July 2023 and only held into August 2024, so 'seasonal high in August 2024' is off on timing, though the level is right.)/T(Francesco di Fano & Claude)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

