<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Highlight/C[1 .8 .25]/P 531 0 R/F 4/QuadPoints[243.21302 115.167118 330.33753 115.167118 243.21302 104.40961 330.33753 104.40961]/Rect[240.67736 103.73726 332.87318 115.83946]/AP<</N 1029 0 R>>/NM(fitz-A0)/Contents(Two things on IBCL. First, its effective duration is ~15.9 years \(BlackRock, mid-June 2026\), not ~17.5, so the table overstates it by about 1.5y. Second, worth stating explicitly: IBCL alone is ~64% of the EUR sleeve's duration. Using the table's own weights and durations, the EUR sleeve runs ~4.9y, the USD sleeve ~3.5y, and the blended book ~4.5y \(~4.3y with the corrected IBCL figure\). Stating that blended number would put a figure behind the 'low beta' claim, which is otherwise asserted rather than shown.)/T(Francesco di Fano & Claude)/BM/Multiply>>
endobj

